    "description": "The film, created in exile from 1971 to 1973 between Cuba and Rome, is considered a \"semi-finished\" work by Glauber Rocha. It has a certain pedagogical character and seeks, through dialectical editing, to conduct a critical review of colonization, class struggle, messianism, and the establishment of populist governments in the Third World. There is a chronology in the events presented, which, supported by extensive iconography (films, engravings, photos, etc.), create \"free\" associations that allow the viewer a \"polyphonic\" view of the \"History of Brazil.\"",
